# Keep LF in the working copy on Windows too.
#
# core.autocrlf is on globally on this machine, so a fresh clone would check
# public/_headers out with CRLF — and _headers is a line-oriented format parsed
# by Cloudflare, not by git. Rather than find out whether its parser tolerates
# stray \r in a header VALUE, pin the whole repo to LF. Nothing here is edited by
# a tool that needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
